What will be printed when the following interface-related code is executed?

```java
interface Drawable {
    int SIZE = 100;
}
public class Main implements Drawable {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(SIZE);
    }
}
```

What will happen when you try to compile and run the following code involving abstract classes?

```java
abstract class Shape {
    abstract void draw();
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Shape s = new Shape();
    }
}
```
